WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.860
Most Star Trek fans can agree that there are
few characters in the series quite as revered

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.160
as The Next Generation's Captain Jean-Luc
Picard.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:08.760
“Isn’t there something else you have to
do?”

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.540
Now, we've finally gotten some concrete news
on Patrick Stewart's return to Starfleet in

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.639
Star Trek: Picard.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:19.720
While the producers of Star Trek: Picard have
been surprisingly forthcoming with info regarding

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.229
the series, mum's the word on when exactly
the series will be beaming onto the CBS All

00:00:24.229 --> 00:00:25.740
Access streaming platform.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:30.060
That will come as a bit of a bummer for die
hard Picard fans who've been waiting since

00:00:30.079 --> 00:00:34.730
2002's disappointing tenth Star Trek movie,
Star Trek: Nemesis, to see what's become of

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:35.780
their beloved Captain.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.070
But even if the exact premiere date of Star
Trek: Picard was not revealed in that Hall

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:44.879
H information dump at San Diego Comic-Con,
the show's producers did unveil the full trailer

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:48.890
for the series, which promises that Picard
will once again boldly go where no man has

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:54.260
gone before sometime in 2020 — plenty of
time to run through all of TNG again, and

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.400
even knock out a little Deep Space Nine as
well.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.160
Maybe skip the movies though.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.980
TNG is timeless, but the feature-length follow-ups?

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.480
They haven't aged that well.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.960
So far we've got two glimpses of the Picard
series — a brief teaser, and a more involved

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.420
trailer just a few months later.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:13.640
The teaser took us back to Picard's family
vineyard, which he retired to sometime after

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.820
the events of TNG, implying that the show
would be picking up more or less where the

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.580
series left off — movies not included.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:23.970
The full trailer doubled-down on the "Old
Man Picard" concept, giving us a substantial

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.940
peek at the surprising things in store for
the Starfleet icon.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.820
There's a lot to unpack in the trailer, including
some unanswered questions.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.320
It seems that Picard will begin the series
in retirement, making wine in the French countryside.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.920
But he's called back to duty to help a mysterious,
and possibly dangerous young woman, whose

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:43.040
story somehow leads him back to the hallowed
halls of Starfleet.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.500
One of the most pressing questions on the
minds of TNG fans when the news of the Picard

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.280
series broke was when exactly the series would
take place.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.320
"5,000 years in the future."

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.280
It's been almost 20 years since we last saw
Picard on the bridge of the Enterprise, in

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:03.120
2002 with TNG's cinematic swan song, Star
Trek: Nemesis - no one's favorite Star Trek

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:03.620
movie.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.780
When we last left the crew, they'd narrowly
escaped a galactic beatdown at the hands of

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.680
the ruthless Picard clone Shinzon.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.900
They'd also seen Jonathan Frakes' Will Riker
leave the Enterprise to take command of the

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.860
USS Titan, and witnessed the tragic demise
of Brent Spiner's Data.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:22.660
Matching up with the real-life time gap, the
Picard series will take place about two decades

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.040
after the events of Nemesis.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:28.840
The years away may not have been particularly
kind to Jean-Luc, who seems more than a little

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.120
haunted in his retirement, with apparently
no one but a new pet dog keeping him company.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:37.480
So it's probably good news for Picard that
the peculiar young woman shows up and sets

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:40.340
him on a more adventurous path, with a whole
new crew to command.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.540
Picard won't be returning to the bridge of
the Enterprise with his TNG crew in tow.

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:49.420
The captain's former crew are likely still
around; they've just moved onto new things,

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.200
and new adventures in the years since they
worked as Starfleet officers under Picard's

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:53.700
command.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.320
As it happens, Picard may not be rolling with
Starfleet at all for this new, secretive mission.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:03.440
While we're not 100% certain how or if Picard
will return to Starfleet proper, we know that

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.490
he'll get a new ship to command, evidently
with a whole new crew of fresh faces from

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.340
Starfleet's next next generation.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:13.340
We don't know much about the crew yet, but
there are some talented actors bringing the

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.380
characters to life.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:19.600
The new faces include Santiago Cabrera from
Big Little Lies as Cristobal Rios, Alison

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:25.240
Pill from Scott Pilgrim vs. The World as Dr.
Agnes Jurati, Michelle Hurd from Ash vs. Evil

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:30.130
Dead as Raffi Musiker, Harry Treadaway from
Penny Dreadful as Narek, and newcomer Evan

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:31.960
Evagora as the Romulan Elnor.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.320
So you can rest assured that there will be
plenty of intrigue among the show's supporting

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:36.820
players.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.640
The show may be called Picard, but with a
cast like this, it looks like it won't be

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:41.940
just about him.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:47.440
We've long suspected that at least a few ghosts
of Star Treks past would be making appearances

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:47.940
in Picard.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:53.470
The series' first full trailer confirmed two
surprising additions to the cast: TNG's Data,

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:57.550
last seen being blown to pieces in the cold
vacuum of space, and Star Trek: Voyager's

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.480
Seven of Nine, last seen… well, on Voyager.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.430
Needless to say, fans have a few questions
about how these two characters will fit into

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.580
the Picard series.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:09.000
"I'm just a man who is looking for answers."

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.040
On one level, the return of Brent Spiner's
inquisitive android makes sense.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:17.920
Data was one of TNG's best-loved characters,
who developed a complex and rich relationship

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.480
with Picard over the course of that show's
seven seasons.

00:04:20.989 --> 00:04:25.200
But with the character apparently having died
at the end of Nemesis, how is he returning,

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:25.700
and why?

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.780
It's hinted at the movie's end that the identical
android B-4 can access Data's personality

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.500
and memories, but is that what's happening
in Picard?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.680
"I do not know."

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.900
As for Seven of Nine, we frankly don't have
a clue what role she'll play in the Picard

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:42.090
series, because she and Picard have never
shared the screen before.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.520
But they do both share the struggle of having
once been part of the Borg Collective.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:50.100
What we do know is that a Borg ship is prominently
featured in the trailer, so there's the potential

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.600
that Seven of Nine will offer some insight
on the state of her former Collective.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:58.180
However she factors into Picard, it's nice
to have Jeri Ryan back in character, as she

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.260
was frequently the most interesting part of
Star Trek: Voyager.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.940
"The robot has been neutralized.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.240
May I leave now?"

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:10.140
Along with Spiner and Ryan, we now know Jonathan
Del Arco will also appear, reprising his role

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.520
as Borg scout Hugh from The Next Generation.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:17.220
For those who don't remember Hugh's memorable
TNG arc, the Borg scout was found stranded

00:05:17.229 --> 00:05:18.949
and critically injured in deep space.

00:05:18.949 --> 00:05:22.980
He was brought aboard the Enterprise, under
protest from Picard, and nursed back to health.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.340
Picard initially sought to use Hugh as a weapon
to destroy the Borg once and for all, but

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:32.540
Hugh's surprising ability to comprehend human
individuality led Picard to cancel his xenocidal

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.040
plans.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.540
Though he doesn't show up in the trailer,
it's been confirmed that TNG alum Jonathan

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:41.230
Frakes will indeed appear on screen as the
Captain Picard's trusted "Number One," Will

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:41.720
Riker.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.240
He'll also be directing some episodes of the
show.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:45.380
"You are correct.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:46.500
It's fact."

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:51.320
Frakes will also be joined on screen by Marina
Sirtis, the Betazoid Deanna Troi.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.599
Hey, anyone know what Levar Burton, Gates
McFadden, and Michael Dorn are up to?

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.310
'Cause it sure feels like Picard is trying
to get the TNG band back together.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.020
"To absent friends."

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.780
Of all the questions raised by the Picard
trailer, one of the biggest surrounds the

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:09.800
identity of a whole new character - the mystery
woman Picard is trying to help.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:14.380
After a two-decade absence, one assumes that
not just anybody could lead Picard back to

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:14.880
Starfleet.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.860
Deepening the mystery, the woman appears to
have a particular affinity for Jean-Luc.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.480
"She came to me for help."

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:24.620
Of course, we promptly see her putting the
smack down on a couple of armed guards, and

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:28.180
we also get some ominous warnings about her
from a couple of characters, so we're not

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.900
entirely sure how much protection she actually
needs.

00:06:31.569 --> 00:06:35.060
For now, that's really all we know about the
new character, outside of the fact that her

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.040
name is Dahj.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.979
She's played by actress Isa Briones.

00:06:38.979 --> 00:06:43.620
Aside from a "blink and you'll miss it" appearance
in 2018's Assassination of Gianni Versace

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:47.990
series, she doesn't have many big credits
to her name, so here's hoping she gets a chance

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:49.940
to make the most of her Star Trek debut.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:55.919
Over his legendary career with Starfleet,
Picard went toe-to-toe with quite a few antagonists,

00:06:55.919 --> 00:07:00.520
from the domineering Borg to the mischievous
Q. As far as who Jean-Luc and company will

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:05.370
be facing off against in Star Trek: Picard,
we still aren't entirely sure - but it's tempting

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:06.660
to think it's the Borg.

00:07:07.069 --> 00:07:11.340
We clearly see one of those dreaded Borg cubes
in the trailer, and Picard also has a very

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.620
specific past with the fearsome Collective.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:17.530
And appearances by Seven of Nine and Hugh
would lead us to think the Borg will figure

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:21.320
prominently in whatever interstellar ruckus
Picard finds himself entwined in.

00:07:21.789 --> 00:07:26.459
But the trailer also gives us clear shots
of what appear to be re-designed Romulan warbirds

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.780
- ships from a species Picard has more than
a prickly past with.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:33.480
It will be interesting to see what shifts
there have been in the status quo since the

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.340
last time we visited the Alpha Quadrant with
Jean-Luc.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.039
Will Picard find himself in another standoff
with the Borg?

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.840
Are the Romulans trying to make a fearsome
comeback?

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:43.550
Is Shinzon back as well???

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.600
For now, we'll just have to wait and see.

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:50.620
While Picard is technically picking up where
The Next Generation left off, the series has

00:07:50.629 --> 00:07:55.029
more in common, both in its look and behind
the scenes, with the other modern-day Star

00:07:55.029 --> 00:07:56.700
Trek series: Star Trek Discovery.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:01.220
Both series are being produced by Alex Kurtzman,
and the shows are also set to be streaming

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:05.860
partners on the CBS All Access platform, with
Picard seemingly taking the same stylishly

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:08.780
cinematic approach to Star Trek as Discovery
does.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:12.460
And Star Trek has never been a series to shy
away from a crossover, either.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:17.560
Many fans are wondering, will Picard and Disco's
disparate crews cross paths on the small screen?

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.120
"I'm not certain of that now, Captain."

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:24.820
While CBS may have some sort of crossover
in mind down the road for these two Star Trek

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:28.940
shows, it's a safe bet that Picard and Discovery
won't intertwine immediately.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:33.460
A lot of that has to do with the current plot
arc of Discovery, going into its third season

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:36.880
- so here's your spoiler warning if you haven't
seen what's up yet.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:41.120
After a head-spinning twist in the season
two finale that saw Discovery's crew leap

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:46.000
1,000 years into the future via a time-spanning
wormhole, the timelines of the two series

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.411
would seem to be way too far apart for a crossover
to work - not that that's stopped the series

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.080
in the past.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:55.640
So while we wouldn't be surprised if the series
collided sometime down the road, it seems

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.720
likely that we'll have to wait for Picard
to find its sea legs first.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:00.260
Maybe in a second season.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.360
But we might be getting ahead of ourselves.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:07.510
With Picard's first season yet to have a launch
date, it's still a little early to speculate

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:09.240
about a potential season two.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:13.320
The series will be starting off with a ten-episode
run, following plot threads that have yet

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.520
to be fully revealed.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:18.930
But though a lot about the series' nitty-gritty
details remains unknown, there seems to be

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:23.320
a lot of goodwill for the nostalgia-inducing
series, considering just how beloved Picard

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:25.330
is as a character - for now, at least.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:29.040
If things go well for the series, and the
show goes over with the fans, there's every

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.030
reason to think a second season is in the
cards.

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.640
But part of that decision rests on the fans,
and how audiences respond to the series.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:38.970
Will viewers respond well to seeing Picard
take to the stars again?

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:42.420
Or will they end up feeling like everyone
should've just let the guy stay retired?

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.460
Either way, the show's fate is in your hands.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:50.120
If you want Picard to continue on after these
initial episodes, you'll have to make it so.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:52.700
"You are a truly clever person."

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:55.480
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:58.660
Plus, even more Looper videos about Star Trek
are coming soon.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.220
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

